# Inspect LaTeX, not English PDFs

This rule is for the agent, not the user. When checking, comparing, or editing a translation, read the `.tex` files. Do not treat compiled English PDFs (for example `Tyranids 300/main.pdf` or `Rulebook 303/main.pdf`) as current. Those PDFs may not have been rebuilt.

The user inspects PDFs they rebuild themselves. Do not ask them to read `.tex`. At inspection gates, remind them to rebuild so they are not looking at a stale PDF.

French originals in `Originals/` are the source documents and should be compared against the LaTeX.

Do not assume an existing English PDF matches the `.tex`.
